cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "bioproc: a notebook workbench for biopharmaceutical process development"
abstract: >-
  An interactive notebook and Python package covering upstream fed-batch mammalian
  cell culture (unstructured Monod-type kinetics with feedback feeding), downstream
  purification (lumped kinetic model for Protein A capture, polishing, viral
  filtration, UF/DF), and the data-driven layer on top: PLS/random-forest/Gaussian-
  process models of batch KPIs, a Raman soft sensor, a serial hybrid model, global
  Sobol sensitivity and Monte Carlo uncertainty. Every model score is reported next to
  a no-information baseline on batch-grouped splits, and every run is verified against
  analytic solutions and mass balances before results are shown.
